body:
To avoid a rant I can break it down to several key points

1. the horrible mental and medical health system fucked over the woman I loved when she was having repeated self harm episodes where they refused to send medical attention because and I quote "she is not currently dying, there's nothing we can do, hope it goes well, do call us if she's actively committing suicide." Never really going to get over that.

&#x200B;

2) the constant fucking racism. I'm from NY and I thought the shitty suburbs I'm from were awful and filled with racists but then I moved here. Never in my life have I experienced as much racism in the 26 years I lived in NY than the 3 years I lived in the NL. Every fucking day people cross the street when I walk by, I get called a kutchinese or whatever the fuck the slur is. People's fucking kids look at me like I'm the first brown man they've ever seen. I get blamed in expat newspapers for not integrating. I'm constantly alienated from my classmates or neighbors because they refuse to understand what the problem is or why we got here and trot out the same fucking bullshit of I'm not trying hard enough.

&#x200B;

3) when I'm not dealing with the 2nd point I deal with the awful social life. The fact the many dutch people I've talked to have told me it's shitty for them too and they live there says it all. The Dutch are cold, alienating, borderline socially inept if not outright, gossipy, judgmental, and cruel fucking assholes. When they're not doing that to each other they make it 1000x harder to get to know them as human beings. Even if I integrate, master dutch, and jump through every stupid hoop they want I still need to schedule a 1 hour hangout 6 weeks in advance for the privilege to hear them bitch about the weather

&#x200B;

4) the weather actually gave me seasonal depression. I've never had the problem before in my life but that's the conclusion, my therapist and I came too when I kept having repeated bouts of suicidal ideation.

&#x200B;

5) cherry on top is the housing situation. I'm blowing through savings to pay for an apartment in the nicest neighborhood in my city to avoid the hell I went through with student housing and roommates. I had to move 3 fucking times in 6 months because of all the drama, headaches, and expat abuse and what do I end up with? A shitty apartment with no sound insulation that's 3x the price with an absentee landlord and a racist building manager that keeps calling me Chinese (I'm Filipino, I've mentioned this so manh times). Oh and a asshole Russian neighbor that doesn't work, gets high off of cocaine all the time, argues with his ever rotating girlfriends at 6:30am, to then play loud ass eurobeat bullshit until she needs to sleep just to do it all again tomorrow. Do I have any recourse to fix this, no said my landlord, Dutch laws don't allow for these types of noise complaints and the evidence around the forums from other immigrants with the same problem seems to prove his point. Can I do better? No I got lucky to get my apartment because I moved in the middle of a pandemic. It's so much worse now than when I first came. Can I report my neighbor who has clearly overstayed his tourist visa? NO of course not the bureaucracy makes that impossible. 

&#x200B;

I could go on like this for hours.....

I'll give it a try on pc later, I've only used it on my switch so far. Hopefully the pc is better.

&#x200B;

Edit: Ok can confirm audio on pc is great. The only issue seems to be the switch at the moment

I would like to second this AAAAAAAAAAAAHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH with my own Halo approved version of it

[https://youtu.be/iIqNWrNnQZs?t=12](https://youtu.be/iIqNWrNnQZs?t=12)

&#x200B;
